{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread","id":1195852,"title":"The Scion: Hero error/question thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-15T14:40:30-07:00","id":1195852,"title":"The Scion: Hero error/question thread","content":"Well, nobody else has started one, so I guess it's mine to start?<br /> <br /> 1. Guide Asset Skills: Described as &quot;as Path Asset Skills, but the Scion doesn't get +1 to these&quot;, but I can't find where that is clarified. The Crane Guide seems to indicate that you get a bonus to Athletics and/or Pilot, but not if the +1 bonus isn't a thing.<br /> 2. Relics and magic for pregen characters: Eric and Emmanuel have Birthrights and Boons, but they don't have ranks shown for their three Callings. Hassan, Rashmi, and Rhiannon look like they still have their Origins character sheets: Only one Calling, no Birthrights, and no Boons.<br /> 3. Character creation inconsistency: Some sections say 4 points in Callings, but Neal stated elsewhere that characters should have 5 points total.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T15:18:45-07:00","id":1195866,"title":"","content":"The Netjer use their proper names in their chapter, and their Greek names in their entire rest of the book.<br /> <br /> Set gets mentiomed under the Relationships section of the Aesir Pantheon, rather than under the Other Pantheons header.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T15:39:31-07:00","id":1195872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1195866#post1195866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Netjer use their proper names in their chapter, and their Greek names in their entire rest of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite the hill to die on, but you seem to be the only one that cares. It's even mentioned in the book as to why they do this in the &quot;Get Them to the Greek&quot; Side bar. It's the same reasoning as to why they use the Greek names for the Theoi instead of their Roman names. It's what they are most commonly known by modern followers. So I for one am perfectly fine with the game using the names that my players and I will recognize.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T15:56:46-07:00","id":1195876,"title":"","content":"In the callings section they seem to have forgotten the Teotl in each callings list of god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:00:02-07:00","id":1195879,"title":"","content":"A couple smaller ones I noticed.<br /> <br /> The Aesir Pantheon Path in Chapter Two don't actually mention what the Asset Skills for the path are. The Aesir Pantheon Appendix in Origin says that they're Close Combat and Occult, but they should honestly mention that.<br /> <br /> The Teotl Patheon Path has THREE Asset Skills, which are Close Combat, Culture, and Empathy. Not only is this one Skill too many, but in Origin the two Asset Skills for the Teotl are listed as Athletics and Culture. Something to fix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:09:58-07:00","id":1195883,"title":"","content":"My suggestion regarding names: Use popular names in the main sections, because most players will know those. Then include historically accurate names in the pronounciation guide that should also be in the books. Win/Win!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:15:14-07:00","id":1195886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Purple Snit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1195883#post1195883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My suggestion regarding names: Use popular names in the main sections, because most players will know those. Then include historically accurate names in the pronounciation guide that should also be in the books. Win/Win!</div> </div> </div> </div>... You mean the way it already is? They way that Lex is complaining about? That way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:38:53-07:00","id":1195895,"title":"","content":"The Heroic Leader Knacks &quot;Captain of Industry&quot; and &quot;Inspirational Aura&quot; are literally word-for-word identical...I imagine one of them is meant to be different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13182-eltheriond","user":"Eltheriond","date":".  Missed a word 03-15-2018, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13182-eltheriond","name":"Eltheriond","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T16:46:58-07:00","id":1195899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eltheriond</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1195895#post1195895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Heroic Leader Knacks &quot;Captain of Industry&quot; and &quot;Inspirational Aura&quot; are literally word-for-word identical...I imagine one of them is meant to be different?</div> </div> </div> </div>... *Checks*<br /> <br /> That's odd. Inspirational Aura doesn't seem to be in Origin. Maybe Inspirational Aura is an old name that got changed and then got double-pasted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T18:04:27-07:00","id":1195914,"title":"","content":"A very minor thing, but one I was surprised by: gods such as Aphrodite and Freya, both often noted as being noted for their beauty, often above all other things, lack Beauty as a perview. <br /> <br /> This could be intentional, but I found it strange and wanted to mention it in case it was an oversight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24013-amaranth01","name":"Amaranth01","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T18:36:24-07:00","id":1195919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1195872#post1195872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite the hill to die on, but you seem to be the only one that cares. It's even mentioned in the book as to why they do this in the &quot;Get Them to the Greek&quot; Side bar. It's the same reasoning as to why they use the Greek names for the Theoi instead of their Roman names. It's what they are most commonly known by modern followers. So I for one am perfectly fine with the game using the names that my players and I will recognize.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think you are speaking too soon on thinking that no one cares. There is a very good reason that it is and should be consistently the same throughout the book. It is a book that needs to referenced at the table and usability at the table should take precedent over readability and common terminology.<br /> <br /> I have a difficult enough time with the various names that I don't want to have to juggle and waste time looking up various sobriquets just so that I can properly reference the gods that I need to if I am interested in the various story hooks that mention dieties throughout the book.<br /> <br /> I feel that they should choose one naming convention over the other, but they should stick with whichever they choose, because otherwise, the book fails as a reference that I can use at the table. Anything that slows down table reference should be limited as much possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T18:43:39-07:00","id":1195922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amaranth01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1195914#post1195914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A very minor thing, but one I was surprised by: gods such as Aphrodite and Freya, both often noted as being noted for their beauty, often above all other things, lack Beauty as a perview.<br /> <br /> This could be intentional, but I found it strange and wanted to mention it in case it was an oversight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall's aware, from the Discord.<br /> <br /> As in, a few days ago he dropped a comment onto the Discord to the effect of &quot;Oh dangit, I forgot to give Aphrodite Beauty!&quot;<br /> <br /> I think we can safely say that Aphrodite will have Beauty. Freya will as well, I made sure to ask.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-15T21:00:43-07:00","id":1195947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1195919#post1195919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you are speaking too soon on thinking that no one cares. There is a very good reason that it is and should be consistently the same throughout the book. It is a book that needs to referenced at the table and usability at the table should take precedent over readability and common terminology.<br /> <br /> I have a difficult enough time with the various names that I don't want to have to juggle and waste time looking up various sobriquets just so that I can properly reference the gods that I need to if I am interested in the various story hooks that mention dieties throughout the book.<br /> <br /> I feel that they should choose one naming convention over the other, but they should stick with whichever they choose, because otherwise, the book fails as a reference that I can use at the table. Anything that slows down table reference should be limited as much possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you disagree with me as much as you think. I too wish that they had just used one set of names, the Greek ones, and had the ancient Egyptian ones that almost no one who's not an Egyptologist or a hipster uses as secondary titles underneath. Even the few Kemetic's that I know personally use the Greek names for their Gods.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T00:27:23-07:00","id":1195989,"title":"","content":"So, the various Specializable Purviews list how you can narrow your focus down to one aspect of the general Purview... but what about deities like Ganesh or Ra, who have multiple specialties while not being generalists either? How do you get Artistry (Dance, Flower Arranging) as a Scion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T01:07:16-07:00","id":1195993,"title":"","content":"Take relics that give you access to the purview multiple times, same as any other purview I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T10:40:14-07:00","id":1196118,"title":"","content":"One of the Hero PCs has a Knack called Structural Integrity; the only reference I can find for this is that one of the Hulder Custom Knacks in Origin says it functions as per Structural Integrity.<br /> <br /> What is Structural Integrity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T11:27:50-07:00","id":1196141,"title":"","content":"Not sure about asking this since I only skimmed Hero and only glimpsed...<br /> <br /> Signature purviews...<br /> Heka for Netjer...ok<br /> Yoga for Devas though? Wouldn't <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siddhi\" target=\"_blank\">siddhi</a> be more appropriate? (even <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E1%B9%9Addhi\" target=\"_blank\">\u1e5addhi</a> should have a mention I suppose)<br /> <br /> Good to see the &quot;astras&quot; given their due. They're frightening.<br /> <br /> Looking forward to reading this indepth during the weekend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","user":"Shadowflame","date":". 03-16-2018, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T13:08:47-07:00","id":1196187,"title":"","content":"The book references a &quot;Feat of Scale&quot; several times, with the capitalization indicating that it is a formal system term. However, there does not seem to be any definition for the term in either Origin or Hero. <br /> <br /> I had assumed that a Feat of Scale was simply any action to which the Scale mechanic applied. However, when talking about Invoking a Title the book states &quot;her player may spend one Legend to increase Scale by one for that action as a Feat of Scale.&quot; Which seems to imply that the Feat of Scale is the act of increasing your Scale rather than an action that uses that Scale. Either way, a definition or some clarifying language might be in order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6513-maltry","name":"Maltry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T14:11:15-07:00","id":1196223,"title":"","content":"The beginning of the Knacks section states that characters begin with five Knacks, one for each dot in their Callings. However, characters only receive four dots in Callings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6513-maltry","name":"Maltry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T14:19:02-07:00","id":1196224,"title":"","content":"The character creation rules says you start out with two Boons, but the rules on Legend says you get one boon per dot of Legend. That's one thing I noticed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1494-deranged-goblin","name":"Deranged Goblin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T14:23:02-07:00","id":1196225,"title":"","content":"Both of those were clarified elsewhere... you start with 5 Dots of Callings, and 2 Boons, and get a new one every dot of Legend... for five total at Legend 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T14:36:57-07:00","id":1196229,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1etYiuHfHR-nTI5obsKhL44stbRmLkuvw2Z6qae_lbWM\" target=\"_blank\">I should link this here.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T14:52:28-07:00","id":1196234,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I failed to mention that the Calling section *also* lists it at five. So I assume that is the correct number. But the Character Creation text needs to be updated. And as Deranged Goblin said, the chart on Legend seems to imply that it is listing the total number of boons that you should have, rather than that number +1. So the devs may want to clarify the text or make a note beneath the chart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6513-maltry","name":"Maltry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6513_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T15:50:02-07:00","id":1196256,"title":"","content":"Phoebe and Rhea both are listed as having Virtues (Foresight and Endurance, respectively) that don't exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T21:50:22-07:00","id":1196364,"title":"","content":"The Liminal Calling lists Manipulation as one of its skills, but that's an attribute.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12689-creepyshutin","name":"CreepyShutIn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T23:29:55-07:00","id":1196381,"title":"","content":"There are a few references to an &quot;Armored&quot; tag for armor in a few places that doesn't actually seem to be listed anywhere in the actual tags list for armor, such as on the nearby sample for a motorcycle jacket.<br /> <br /> For that matter, it would be nice if there were a slightly more clear guide on if there was something weapons granted besides their tags. Like, say my Scion of Hachiman has a finely wrought yumi bow that isn't a Relic. Would that be a +1 equipment enhancement? Greater? Not an enhancement at all and only affected by its tags? I kind of wish the Quality tag from the Trinity previews was a thing here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Won't you believe in him? Even if there is no God, or Buddha...there is still Kamen Rider.&quot; \u2014Taki Kazuya, <i>Kamen Rider SPIRITS</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">Now...count up </span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">all your sins.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/160-cyclonejoker","name":"CycloneJoker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar160_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T06:14:03-07:00","id":1196457,"title":"","content":"So, I'm a little confused about Creature Birthrights.<br /> <br /> Hero has the following text in that section:<br /> Examples have been provided in Chapter 6: Storyguiding (p. XX),<br /> listed by how many dots in the Creature Birthright would be required to obtain that creature as a<br /> companion.<br /> <br /> However, I can't find those examples.<br /> <br /> Trying to extrapolate from the guidance given would suggest looking at Flairs + Primary Pool. Would Qualities also be included? Or do Creatures just get all of their qualities? Consider the Nemean Lion: Is it Creature 3 (9 Pool + 0 Flairs) or Creature 5 (9 Pool + 0 Flairs + 3 Qualities)?<br /> <br /> Further confusing things is that the Building the Creature section of Hero suggests Miasmic Presence as an example of a Flair/Knack, listed as a Sandbag in Origin, and a Quality in the Antagonist examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T21:28:35-07:00","id":1196707,"title":"","content":"Confused about this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Transfigure Boon from the Theoi's Metamorphosis purview</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>At the end of this Boon</i>, Scions and other characters with Legend 1+ instantly revert to their true form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Transfigure's duration is Instant, so it basically doesn't work on anything with Legend as they revert immediately? I don't think that was the intention, since it would be simpler to just say it doesn't work on beings with Legend if that was the case. I'm guessing it is supposed to last a scene in this case, but would love clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T21:15:59-07:00","id":1198241,"title":"","content":"Page 9 of the PDF under Ukemochi no Kami, it says &quot;Ukemochi vomited for the tastiest rice for Tsukiyomi, the mood God, who felt disrespected and struck her down.&quot; Admittedly, it seems like he's a pretty moody god, but I assume this is a typo. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T16:53:13-07:00","id":1199533,"title":"","content":"Origins and Hero both mention Fatigue, but then never go on to give them a condition or effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24031-irhfa","name":"IRHFA","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-25T17:05:33-07:00","id":1199540,"title":"","content":"Hero under the description of the Trickster Calling replaced Failure Deed and Adoption Deed with Crises<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1196707#post1196707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Confused about this:<br /> Well, Transfigure's duration is Instant, so it basically doesn't work on anything with Legend as they revert immediately? I don't think that was the intention, since it would be simpler to just say it doesn't work on beings with Legend if that was the case. I'm guessing it is supposed to last a scene in this case, but would love clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there are two durations to take into account. I believe that the instant duration is to note the time it take for the character to be transformed. Though you are correct that in that it would be nice for the duration of the transformation itself to be clarified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T06:39:54-07:00","id":1200784,"title":"","content":"IIRC Sarutahiko has 4 callings listed in hero instead of the three everyone else gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T15:06:37-07:00","id":1201428,"title":"","content":"Again sorry for multi-posting. <br /> <br /> Should Ogun's forge purview be specialized considering he's the god of Iron? I figure he'd have Forge (Metallurgy) like how Susan-O has it. <br /> <br /> Under the description of The Visitation it has the following text, &quot;Ganesh riding in on a mouse to welcome his child to the Sh\u00e9n,&quot;. Ganesh aka Ganesha is not a member of the Shen so I'm unsure whether it's the pantheon or the god's name that is incorrect in that instance, unless there is a Shen god named Ganesh that went unmentioned in Hero. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T17:33:00-07:00","id":1201759,"title":"","content":"\u200bIn the part of the System chapter talking about the Trickster calling, it mentions that the path's crises include getting caught in your own trick or being outsmarted. Are the crises analogous to failure deeds? And don't all established Tricksters get outsmarted in a fair few of their stories - are the Heroes being punished for something that the gods do all the time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13499-not-quite-yoda","name":"Not Quite Yoda","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-01T11:51:34-07:00","id":1201983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Not Quite Yoda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1201759#post1201759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bIn the part of the System chapter talking about the Trickster calling, it mentions that the path's crises include getting caught in your own trick or being outsmarted. Are the crises analogous to failure deeds? And don't all established Tricksters get outsmarted in a fair few of their stories - are the Heroes being punished for something that the gods do all the time?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Failure Deed and a Crisis are indeed basically the same thing. It's something <i>can</i> let you swap out your Trickster Calling... But you don't have to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-03T17:21:50-07:00","id":1202812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GrayWalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1200784#post1200784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC Sarutahiko has 4 callings listed in hero instead of the three everyone else gets.</div> </div> </div> </div>He does, for some reason he has Liminal, Lover, Sage, and Warrior.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3653-thegraysoul","name":"TheGraySoul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T00:52:34-07:00","id":1205119,"title":"","content":"So I hope this is the right place to ask this question, but here goes. I noticed in the base Scion: Hero book that under the Egyptian pantheon that among them that the god Geb has a listing for no Epic Attributes. Does anyone have any idea what these might be?<br /> <br /> Also does anyone know why none of the Amatsukami have access to the Justice or Fire purviews?<br /> <br /> Now again this is for first edition not second so I hope I'm putting this in the right spot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-10T07:23:03-07:00","id":1205190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1205119#post1205119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I hope this is the right place to ask this question, but here goes. I noticed in the base Scion: Hero book that under the Egyptian pantheon that among them that the god Geb has a listing for no Epic Attributes. Does anyone have any idea what these might be?<br /> <br /> Also does anyone know why none of the Amatsukami have access to the Justice or Fire purviews?<br /> <br /> Now again this is for first edition not second so I hope I'm putting this in the right spot.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This thread is for the Second Edition of Hero. You might have more luck in the &quot;Ask Neall&quot; thread or starting a new discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T00:32:32-07:00","id":1205485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1205119#post1205119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also does anyone know why none of the Amatsukami have access to the Justice or Fire purviews?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't Amaterasu have Justice? And none of them have fire for the simple reason that none of them are Fire Gods. They still don't have Fire in 2e either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T05:09:15-07:00","id":1205540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1205485#post1205485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't Amaterasu have Justice? And none of them have fire for the simple reason that none of them are Fire Gods. They still don't have Fire in 2e either.</div> </div> </div> </div> To answer your first question. No Amaterasu does not have the Justice purview in 1st Edition. They might have given it to her in 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> As to the second response actually yes the Japanese pantheon does have deities related to fire. The first of which us Kagasuchi. Now yes I'm aware he's a Titan Spawn. However there IS another one. His successor. Where as Kagasuchi is the raw destructive power of fire in that simply burns indiscrimently.(And is also the patron deity of blacksmiths in Japan?) Kojin the God of Fire, Hearth and the Kitchen represents the raw destructive power of fire when turned to the betterment of man kind. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K\u014djin\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K\u014djin</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T06:05:06-07:00","id":1205555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1205540#post1205540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To answer your first question. No Amaterasu does not have the Justice purview in 1st Edition. They might have given it to her in 2nd Edition.<br /> <br /> As to the second response actually yes the Japanese pantheon does have deities related to fire. The first of which us Kagasuchi. Now yes I'm aware he's a Titan Spawn. However there IS another one. His successor. Where as Kagasuchi is the raw destructive power of fire in that simply burns indiscrimently.(And is also the patron deity of blacksmiths in Japan?) Kojin the God of Fire, Hearth and the Kitchen represents the raw destructive power of fire when turned to the betterment of man kind. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K\u014djin\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K\u014djin</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry if I was unclear... I meant that none of the Gods that are part of the Amatsukami <i>write-up</i> are Fire Gods. Given the sheer number of Kami, they couldn't possibly have written them all up and while 2nd Edition has a vastly expanded roster, Kojin is still not there. There are slated to be additional Patrons per Pantheon in the Companion though, so maybe he'll be there.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, Amaterasu has the Order Purview in 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 04-11-2018, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T12:21:24-07:00","id":1205707,"title":"","content":"So Order is replacing Justice in 2ed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T12:30:32-07:00","id":1205709,"title":"","content":"If we want to get really technical. I think the Judge calling is replacing the Justice purview with Order taking care of whats left.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T20:19:17-07:00","id":1205887,"title":"","content":"Ugh not sure I am liking that idea. Order is not Justice. It smells like they are trying to streamline to the point of making everything so homoginized(Which if I spelled that wrong I apologize for it.) that it loses much of the flavor that made playing it fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T21:15:57-07:00","id":1205907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1205887#post1205887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ugh not sure I am liking that idea. Order is not Justice. It smells like they are trying to streamline to the point of making everything so homoginized(Which if I spelled that wrong I apologize for it.) that it loses much of the flavor that made playing it fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's sort of the opposite of being streamlined actually. Order is not Justice, that is why they broke it apart. Where in 1e Justice was a single Purview for Tyranny, Kingship, Oathkeeping, Political Legitimacy, Investigations, the Law, and many other concepts, these have been broken into different parts an individual Scion could chose to represent.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to play someone who gives Kingship out to whomsoever they please, you would take Order. If you want to be a perfect fair and just ruler, you can do this through Order, Judge, and Leader. If you want to be a detective, you only need Judge, but you could take Order if you want. The Irish Brehon for instance would have only had Judge, and probably Sage since they were the keepers of the law, not the law itself.<br /> <br /> By dividing these concepts up, the game has made itself more complex, but also allowed for more complex characters. Instead of a queen taking Justice, now they could take Leader and Order, meaning that they are something like an unquestionable Divine Monarch who does not bother with the law save that They Are The Law. A king could take Judge and Leader, a ruler who is bound and fettered by the law, who wields the law as it is, but is not a living embodiment of it. Another king may only take Leader, and have no actual capacity to interact with the law (such as Bres from Irish saga literature).<br /> <br /> Think of it less that Order replaces Justice, but Justice has been broken apart into Order, Judge, and parts of Leader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-11T22:48:26-07:00","id":1205938,"title":"","content":"Eh...the more I'm hearing about 2nd Ed the less and less I'm liking what I'm hearing about it. For me I'm just going to view it was changing something that honestly didn't need to be changed for the sake of changing it. About the only things I might take away from 2nd Ed. are the new deities. That's about it.<br /> <br /> By the way I know that sounds like I'm being rude and contrite for the sake of being contrite. I'm not. I just don't exactly see the point of changing something that honestly didn't need changing. Justice was always a very simple concept. When applied correctly justice is fair. Which I guess why should I discard one thing just because I don't need it? They are all parts of a greater whole. When you discard one you diminish the whole. At least that's my opinion.<br /> <br /> Which I am still curious why they got rid of gods like Izanagi, Izanami, Geb, Kalfu, Damballa and Baron Samedi? As I can't seemed to find those deities listed in the new pantheon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","user":"Sessha","date":". 04-12-2018, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T00:07:19-07:00","id":1205957,"title":"","content":"Umm...first edition was broken. There were many mechanics that were completely unbalanced, rules that didn't work, and information that was inaccurate. It desperately needed an overhaul - it is most definitely something that needed to be changed. And several of the gods you mention are either of questionable providence (Kalfu, Baron Samedi) or not central enough to the pantheons to warrant inclusion at this point, and so were left out deliberately. Honestly, if you liked 1st edition, stick with it. But 2nd edition isn't just &quot;change for the sake of change&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T01:00:56-07:00","id":1205962,"title":"","content":"Okay...let me see if I can quantify this without turning this thread into a flame war. Which believe me is the last thing I want to do.<br /> <br /> First off I'll start by meeting you halfway on things. Yes I do agree that many of rules needed an overhaul. Heck I even noticed a bit of double talk in the application of two different knacks in the demigod book. One of them said it did one thing and the other was suppose to cover what that one did as well. Then they turn around in the last paragraph of the knack's description and about counter it by saying something else. If you were wonder what I'm referring to that's the knack in the epic wits section Eternal Vigilance and Cobra Reflexes. If you want to read further on that I do not doubt that info is available.<br /> <br /> The mere fact that one of the Deities in Egyptian Pantheon had no epic attributes!~?(...yeah that needed fixing badly.) Also some of the Pantheon specific purviews were not powerful or as useful as others. The Norse comes to mind as one of the more useless ones.(At least as far I could see.) The Aztecs' and Egyptians were kind of useful. As was the Greek and the Japanese and the Loa to one degree or another. Heck I'm still trying figure out the initiative system. Plus the way the health levels and such were applied seemed horribly unbalanced in favor of the enemies.(Which in a way I guess is the point. Epic storytelling and all that such)<br /> <br /> Also the virtue system could desperately use and overhaul. It's so nebulous that yeah it needs clarification. With a simple application of logic you can wiggle your way out of most of them without having to roll.<br /> <br /> I'll also even admit that based on the White Wolf system the Epic Attributes...were horribly broken and arguably more powerful than most of the General Purpose Purviews and such. Plus something I noticed was again double talk in reference to when Scions finally reach godhood. The book even says that when a scion reaches godhood any and all epic attributes for which he has the required level in,(which is 8) automatically become associated with him. Otherwise those associated with him are those of his parent deity Which is interesting since you attain godhood at legend 9. What this means that you can never have your epic attributes at a high enough level when you reach godhood to ever get them associated with you since when you reach legend 9 your epics are only level 7. Then they turn around in the same paragraph(again) and say it only matters at the time of a scion visitation and such. That doesn't make sense to me in the slightest.<br /> <br /> Which by the way I was all in favor of new deities being added. Hell I've even stated to others they should have released something like a pantheon book or something that took all the gods and goddesses they added over the course the books and added them in. Plus adding in more deities would have been fun as well. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So yes in ways I can see your point that the system was broken(badly in some cases) enough to warrant an overhaul. However the breaking up of some purviews like that seems to me completely unnecessary and was a change for the sake of change. To me things like Judge or Order or Leader are all things that encompassed by Justice. Well maybe not Leader(Fail to see how that works) In my view breaking them up doesn't create more dynamic characters it feels like a watering down to me.<br /> <br /> Again these are my opinions. Which leads again into my next statement. I want to offer my sincerest apologies for my earlier comments and how disrespectful they were. I am not trying to bash the new system, but I as a person do not like the new way they decided to break some of the things up in the new edition. It just doesn't feel right to me. Once more I offer you, Purple Snit my sincere apologies for my earlier disrespectful comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T06:57:56-07:00","id":1206010,"title":"","content":"I didn't take them as disrespectful, it just sounded like you were writing off second edition as unnecesary, which it isn't. If you don't like breaking up Justice, you can make a house rule about it, but it just seems like a minor reason to write off the new game. No offense was taken on my part - everyone is entitled to an opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T18:11:34-07:00","id":1206210,"title":"","content":"Editing: I was tired and frustrated when I posted this. I'm not 100% on the game as-presented, but I'm closer to happy than I am to throw-my-hands-up.<br /> <br /> I think a good round of editing will do the game some good and alleviate most of my issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8985-gnomeborg","user":"Gnomeborg","date":". 04-13-2018, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8985-gnomeborg","name":"Gnomeborg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-12T18:25:16-07:00","id":1206215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomeborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1206210#post1206210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... and we don't even have a list of skills....</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit the placement might have been a little better, but there is a list of skills (with descriptions) in Scion: Origin on about pg 60 in Ch 2 after the description of the core mechanic and before the discussion of Arenas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1039-brennanhawkwood","name":"Brennanhawkwood","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T01:57:46-07:00","id":1206346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1205938#post1205938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh...the more I'm hearing about 2nd Ed the less and less I'm liking what I'm hearing about it. For me I'm just going to view it was changing something that honestly didn't need to be changed for the sake of changing it. About the only things I might take away from 2nd Ed. are the new deities. That's about it.<br /> <br /> By the way I know that sounds like I'm being rude and contrite for the sake of being contrite. I'm not. I just don't exactly see the point of changing something that honestly didn't need changing. Justice was always a very simple concept. When applied correctly justice is fair. Which I guess why should I discard one thing just because I don't need it? They are all parts of a greater whole. When you discard one you diminish the whole. At least that's my opinion.<br /> <br /> Which I am still curious why they got rid of gods like Izanagi, Izanami, Geb, Kalfu, Damballa and Baron Samedi? As I can't seemed to find those deities listed in the new pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Izanami Izanagi and Geb are no longer Gods because 2e creates new classes of deities called Primordial and they fit that classification better. Same thing happened to Brahma of the Deva. Kalfu, Damballa and the Baron aren't in because their pantheon, the Loa, is not in the core. It is slated for inclusion in the Companion, so we will hopefully see them there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T02:12:16-07:00","id":1206350,"title":"","content":"As for the Order Justice thing... You'll be happy to know that nothing has been discarded <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Order is the Purview of divine authority and sovereignty, and the establishment of civilization in opposition to Chaos. Leader is the calling of kings and queens, those who lead while others follow. Judge is the Calling of those who enforce the rules and mete out punishment or reward or mercy as they see fit. A God with Order but no Leader or Judge, like Vishnu, is a force of stability and protector against disorder, but not much for actual laws. A God with Order and Judge, like Lakshmi, is both a force for stability and giver of sovereignty, and also a deity who constantly judges the works of mortals and rewards them with fortune and misfortune as she sees fit. A God with Order and Leader, like Indra, is a classical king who established and embodies the laws of the land, but has underlings to actually enforce them. And a God with all three, like Hera, is a force of divine sovereign power, a queen of the gods, and a judge of fidelity and marriage laws. So, as I hope you can see, nuance has been added, rather than anything being removed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T03:17:47-07:00","id":1206355,"title":"","content":"Alright so I am going to ask this question as it's kind of bugging me because in my mind the idea makes absolutely no sense what so ever. What exactly do they mean by Primordial deities?<br /> <br /> Which stupid question. I'm guessing the reason Ra wasn't in the Egyptian Pantheon listing was because he's been relegated to a primordial do-hicky thing that I don't understand?<br /> <br /> Also I suppose I'll ask now. What other purviews did they include and which ones did they feel the need to dissect, vivisect, amputate, stitch, re-stitch and graft into others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","user":"Sessha","date":". 04-13-2018, 06:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T03:27:46-07:00","id":1206356,"title":"","content":"There are three kinds of deities in Scion 2e... Gods, who are primarily involved with the World through the lens of Callings and humanity... Titans, who primarily interact with the World through, and are consumed by, their Purviews... And Primordials, who are those deities that are distant from and do not involve themselves with the World. Titans in 2e aren't necessarily evil, just completely caught up in their Purviews... Helios for example is a Titan that works with the Greek gods. Ao Kuang the Dragon King of the Eastern Sea works for the Shen... The Orisha as a pantheon don't have any Titans at all. Primordial deities are people like Oludomare of the Orisha or Danu of the Tuatha, who are vast cosmic creator deities that rarely if ever interact with humanity themselves. These classifications are not static... Ra was a Primordial who became a God after Isis stole his name, and Brahma was a God whose steadily weakening relationship with the World as he withdraws into himself have made him a Primordial.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T03:44:07-07:00","id":1206358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1206355#post1206355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which stupid question. I'm guessing the reason Ra wasn't in the Egyptian Pantheon listing was because he's been relegated to a primordial do-hicky thing that I don't understand?<br /> <br /> Also I suppose I'll ask now. What other purviews did they include and which ones did they feel the need to dissect, vivisect, amputate, stitch, re-stitch and graft into others?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ra is but in the Netjer... He's called Re, but he's there. <br /> <br /> Off the top of my head, there are 28 Purviews in 2e : Artistry, Beasts, Beauty, Chaos, Darkness, Death, Deception, Earth, Epic Dexterity, Epic Stamina, Epic Strength, Fertility, Fire, Forge, Fortune, Frost, Health, Journeys, Moon, Order, Passion, Prosperity, Sky, Sun, Stars, War, Water, Wild<br /> <br /> I'll leave it to you to decide what has been 'needlessly' operated upon, but all the powers from 1e are there, and more besides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T03:45:58-07:00","id":1206359,"title":"","content":"Which I have never heard the name Re used to identify with Ra in the slightest. I've heard Atum-Ra and Ra are the two that I know of. Sounds like they just wanted to change it to make it sound more snooty if you ask me.<br /> <br /> I see they blended the epic attributes now together with the Purviews. Most of them are there save one which is still pretty important and such.<br /> <br /> Though fun interesting fact I found while doing some research on Helios. It actually kind of identifies him not as a Titan but as a god. Yes he was birthed by a Titan and a Titaness, but so was Zeus, Hera, Poseidon, Hades and Hestia(?) Oh and of course the rock Rhea fed Chronos in place of Zeus.. Can't forget That Rock. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","user":"Sessha","date":". 04-13-2018, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T03:50:33-07:00","id":1206361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1206359#post1206359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So why did I not see Ra's name listed in the Egyptian Pantheon listing if he is no longer a Primordial Deity? I didn't see any of the names he's known for in any mythologies.<br /> <br /> Though fun interesting fact I found while doing some research on Helios. It actually kind of identifies him not as a Titan but as a god. Yes he was birthed by a Titan and a Titaness, but so was Zeus, Hera, Poseidon, Hades and Hestia(?) Oh and of course the rock Rhea fed Chronos in place of Zeus.. Can't forget That Rock. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Scion terms God and Titan don't always correspond to their usage in Greek myth... The Orisha for example are all gods per the mechanical definition, but will happily tell you that there is only one God, Oludomare, who per Scions definition is a Primordial, not a God.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm copy pasting this from Marin's response to you on the other thread:<br /> Netjer: Anpu, Bast, Het-Heru, Heru, Aset, Khnum, Wesir, Ptah, <b>Re</b>, Set, Sobek, Djehuty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T03:58:44-07:00","id":1206363,"title":"","content":"Yeah I saw your response and edited my post accordingly. I figured you copied it. Like I mentioned above I just didn't recognize the name itself because it's not one I'm familiar with him being called in mythology. Though the other names for some of the deities are ones I've never really heard before so it throws a few people for some loops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T04:04:39-07:00","id":1206364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1206363#post1206363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yeah I saw your response and edited my post accordingly. I figured you copied it. Like I mentioned above I just didn't recognize the name itself because it's not one I'm familiar with him being called in mythology. Though the other names for some of the deities are ones I've never really heard before so it throws a few people for some loops.</div> </div> </div> </div>They used the ancient Egyptian names, they did not randomly make up words to be snooty. The more familiar names are in the aliases under each God.<br /> <br /> Also, literal first line on doing a Google search for Ra God :<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ra or Re is the ancient Egyptian sun god. </div> </div> </div>(Just searching for Ra gets you rheumatic arthritis)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 04-13-2018, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T04:09:45-07:00","id":1206366,"title":"","content":"Well there is just one thing that needs deciding. What sort of status does That Rock hold in the Greek Pantheon? I mean it did spend time in the belly of a Titan so it's got to count for something right? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T04:23:04-07:00","id":1206369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1206359#post1206359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like they just wanted to change it to make it sound more snooty if you ask me.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ra\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Re-Horakhty.svg/960px-Re-Horakhty.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ra\" target=\"_blank\"> Ra - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ra\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ra </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Ra or Re&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://ancientegyptonline.co.uk/ra.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://ancientegyptonline.co.uk/ra.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Page not found | Ancient Egypt Online </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://ancientegyptonline.co.uk/ra.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://ancientegyptonline.co.uk/ra.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Ra (Re)&quot;<br /> <br /> The next two links from a google search for 'ra Egyptian god' don\u2019t mention the alternate spelling- except one does mention it can also be pronounced 'rey', <br /> <br /> If you ask me, it\u2019s bad form to accuse someone of 'just being snooty' when even the most cursory search shows it\u2019s actually a valid spelling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T04:39:15-07:00","id":1206371,"title":"","content":"Again as I have stated before I've never heard the name pronounced in that fashion. In just about every medium I've ever heard used the two most common ones I've heard were of course Ra or Atum-Ra. Hence why to me it sounded like they were being snooty and not wanting to use the more popular names so they can further say they are different from 1st Ed.<br /> <br /> On a different subject. I'm guessing they renamed the Psychopomp to Journeys? And the same for Trickery to Deception?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T04:43:48-07:00","id":1206373,"title":"","content":"Same deal as with the justice purview i think. Psychopomp is in the Liminal calling. Trickery is expanded in the trickster calling and the deception purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T04:56:41-07:00","id":1206377,"title":"","content":"So then it seems to me that every single purview has been bisected, trisected and quadsected before being stitched and re-stitched back into something that sounds like it more convoluted than intelligent all in the name of making it &quot;nuanced&quot; Which sometimes is just a fancy way of saying you changed it for the pure sake of changing something that didn't need to be changed.<br /> <br /> Now on a more serious note. I want to go on record as saying that when I first heard about Scion 2E I was kind of happy as it would mean new stuff and such, but I was also a bit nervous. After all not all change is good change. Then I got to reading and listening to what people were telling me about the new edition and the more I heard about it the less and less I like what I'm hearing. I mean I was quite happy to see so many new deities being added to the mix that honestly should have been there since the game's original inception.<br /> <br /> As I agreed with Stint on the other page Scion needed an overhaul of it's systems I won't lie about that idea. That said this is not the kind of overhaul it needed. What was needed was more in line of going from D&amp;D 3.5 to Pathfinder. Not 3.5 to 4th Ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","user":"Sessha","date":". 04-13-2018, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T04:59:14-07:00","id":1206378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1206371#post1206371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again as I have stated before I've never heard the name pronounced in that fashion. In just about every medium I've ever heard used the two most common ones I've heard were of course Ra or Atum-Ra. Hence why to me it sounded like they were being snooty and not wanting to use the more popular names so they can further say they are different from 1st Ed.<br /> <br /> On a different subject. I'm guessing they renamed the Psychopomp to Journeys? And the same for Trickery to Deception?</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason for that is that the Greek names dominate our discussion of the Egyptian gods, as the Greeks were kind of prolific and very quick to just adopt and take over anything they found interesting, such as...the Egyptian gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T05:21:11-07:00","id":1206386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1206377#post1206377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So then it seems to me that every single purview has been bisected, trisected and quadsected before being stitched and re-stitched back into something that sounds like it more convoluted than intelligent all in the name of making it &amp;quot;nuanced&amp;quot; Which sometimes is just a fancy way of saying you changed it for the pure sake of changing something that didn't need to be changed.<br /> <br /> Now on a more serious note. I want to go on record as saying that when I first heard about Scion 2E I was kind of happy as it would mean new stuff and such, but I was also a bit nervous. After all not all change is good change. Then I got to reading and listening to what people were telling me about the new edition and the more I heard about it the less and less I like what I'm hearing. I mean I was quite happy to see so many new deities being added to the mix that honestly should have been there since the game's original inception.<br /> <br /> As I agreed with Stint on the other page Scion needed an overhaul of it's systems I won't lie about that idea. That said this is not the kind of overhaul it needed. What was needed was more in line of going from D&amp;D 3.5 to Pathfinder. Not 3.5 to 4th Ed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I too am horrified at the great gashes and operation scars that dot the bodies of such Purviews as Earth Fire Sky Water War Health Sun Moon Stars Chaos Frost and Death. And Beasts and Deception, which are the old Animal and Illusion Purviews (incidentally, I don't remember a Trickery purview in 1e, my memory of it may be failing me) just with a different name.<br /> <br /> But honestly, I doubt anything we say will convince you, with or without snark... I wish you luck in your continuing journey in 1e. But, just as a personal opinion... The jump for Scion didn't need to be 3.5 to Pathfinder, it needed to be 1st edition to 5th.<br /> <br /> I'm going to respectfully disagree with your assessment and bow out of this conversation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T05:35:29-07:00","id":1206394,"title":"","content":"Incidentally I have not actually played D&amp;D 5th Ed. After the abysmal experience I had playing 4th Ed. I swore off playing anymore. Which from the stuff I've heard about 5th Edition it feels like a lighter version of 4th Ed.<br /> <br /> On a different note you were right it was Illusion not Trickery. Trickster was the Avatar Expression of the Illusion Purview. So yeah your mind wasn't failing you. Mine was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","user":"Sessha","date":". 04-13-2018, 08:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T07:02:01-07:00","id":1206417,"title":"","content":"It sounds to me like you just dislike change, honestly. They renamed the purviews, yes - they want it to be a new system, and cutting-and-pasting the old names isn't saying &quot;new&quot; to anyone. I'm more concerned with how they work, not what they are called. I'm really not sure exactly what your point and complaints are. Yes, it's different - it is a new edition trying to fix a broken one. No, some of the gods in 1st edition aren't here, but many more are, and better-researched as well. Yes, they are using the correct names for the Egyptians, and others - see &quot;better-researched&quot;. No, it may not be to everyone's liking. If you don't like it, don't buy it. And comparing it to other systems (and criticizing them) is not only kind of pointless, it's likely to annoy the mods. Honestly, like Samudra, I don't have anything else to add. Best of luck with your gaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-13T16:33:52-07:00","id":1206720,"title":"","content":"Sorry about my earlier post, folks. I was getting ready to run character creation for my players, and it had me all sorts of shook, and like a fool, I blamed that on the book and not on myself.<br /> <br /> The game, as-presented, leaves a lot unexplained. But a good round of editing will fix most of that.<br /> <br /> My issues with everything else that I thought were clunky sort of melted away as I explained to friends what I thought was clunky and realized I already understood most of it (other stuff, like the term Calling being used for both Role and Calling, and the interchangeable use of Aspiration instead of Deed, just took a clearer head to figure out, even if they should be cleaned up).<br /> <br /> I'm still a little fuzzy on how invoking a path works, but I think that'll come with just doing it a couple times.<br /> <br /> I'm also still confused about EXP costs, because the chart in Origin makes everything seem astronomically over-priced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8985-gnomeborg","name":"Gnomeborg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T02:41:25-07:00","id":1206834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomeborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1206720#post1206720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also still confused about EXP costs, because the chart in Origin makes everything seem astronomically over-priced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I had the opposite reaction.<br /> <br /> Players should be expecting 4XP per session, minimum (1 for showing up, 1 for achieving their Short-term Deed, 1 for everyone achieving their Short-term Deed, 1 for spending half the Momentum in the pool). That's all entirely within the player's control - They set their Deeds, they control their Momentum, etc. (and you can have multiple Short-term Deeds, so you can hedge your bets).<br /> <br /> And then in any &quot;significant&quot; session for your character, you're going to be picking up some of the extras (Long-term Deed, story milestone, story end, etc.). Assume one of those every 2 or 3 sessions, on average?<br /> <br /> That means you're looking at putting up an Attribute every other session, or picking up a 4 dot Relic in 4 sessions (That's a Relic that grants you two separate Purviews, or grants you a general +2 Enhancements. To put it another way, the equivalent of <i>6 extra dice</i>.). It means that in 2 or 3 sessions, you can grow your single Follower straight past a group (5-10 individuals) into a mob (20-50 people). You're never more than about 5 sessions from having the Golden Stag of Artemis, or from owning Tyrfing.<br /> <br /> And remember, this is just one of your advancement methods. While you're spending experience to pick up Birthrights, or to max out your Skills and Attributes, you're also completing Deeds. And it's that which triggers Legend increasing, and controls Callings and Boons (I.e., where you actually get your big, flashy power).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2649,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","user":"Tarion","date":". 04-14-2018, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2649-tarion","name":"Tarion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-14T19:48:35-07:00","id":1207133,"title":"","content":"This is true. Though there is a point where effort being expended begins to lag behind amount needed. I know in 1st Ed. in order to keep pace you would need to increase the mount of xp given to account for the higher cost of everything. Which the cost for going up with Legend got to monstrous once ou got beyond the hero level and into the demigod level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T00:50:05-07:00","id":1207195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1207133#post1207133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This is true. Though there is a point where effort being expended begins to lag behind amount needed. I know in 1st Ed. in order to keep pace you would need to increase the mount of xp given to account for the higher cost of everything. Which the cost for going up with Legend got to monstrous once ou got beyond the hero level and into the demigod level.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given Scion 2e doesn\u2019t have scaling xp, not really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1596-horngeek","name":"horngeek","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T05:15:52-07:00","id":1207221,"title":"","content":"Okay time to ask the dumb question.(As in dumb on my part for not understanding the context of your statement not that you are dumb or the statement is dumb just the author is dumb for not understanding) What exactly do you mean by no scaling XP?<br /> <br /> I was just going off the idea that when it takes you three to four months to gain enough XP to raise one thing then it might be time to change how much XP you are handing out. Or if the game itself is only happening once every two or three weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T05:46:17-07:00","id":1207228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1207221#post1207221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly do you mean by no scaling XP?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that the XP cost to improve abilities no longer depends on what level those abilities are already at. &quot;Raise an attribute&quot; just has a flat cost, for example, regardless of whether you're raising it from 1 to 2 or 4 to 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Scion 2E</b> Freelancer: <i>Origin; Hero; Demigod; God; Mythical Denizens; Mysteries of the World; Saints &amp; Monsters; No Gods, No Masters; Once &amp; Future, Realms of Magic &amp; Mystery</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/369-geoffrey","name":"Geoffrey","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T06:09:54-07:00","id":1207236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geoffrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1207228#post1207228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It means that the XP cost to improve abilities no longer depends on what level those abilities are already at. &quot;Raise an attribute&quot; just has a flat cost, for example, regardless of whether you're raising it from 1 to 2 or 4 to 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah thank you. On the low end that flat cost kind of sucks but I can see where it gets better on the upper end of the scale. The part of the scle where the cost used to get rather XP intensive to a degree of dumb.Going from legend 8 to 9 in 1st ed...(8)(9)=72 xp...ouch that's a lot of XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T10:11:11-07:00","id":1207313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1206834#post1206834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? I had the opposite reaction.<br /> <br /> Players should be expecting 4XP per session, minimum (1 for showing up, 1 for achieving their Short-term Deed, 1 for everyone achieving their Short-term Deed, 1 for spending half the Momentum in the pool). That's all entirely within the player's control - They set their Deeds, they control their Momentum, etc. (and you can have multiple Short-term Deeds, so you can hedge your bets).<br /> <br /> And then in any &quot;significant&quot; session for your character, you're going to be picking up some of the extras (Long-term Deed, story milestone, story end, etc.). Assume one of those every 2 or 3 sessions, on average?<br /> <br /> That means you're looking at putting up an Attribute every other session, or picking up a 4 dot Relic in 4 sessions (That's a Relic that grants you two separate Purviews, or grants you a general +2 Enhancements. To put it another way, the equivalent of <i>6 extra dice</i>.). It means that in 2 or 3 sessions, you can grow your single Follower straight past a group (5-10 individuals) into a mob (20-50 people). You're never more than about 5 sessions from having the Golden Stag of Artemis, or from owning Tyrfing.<br /> <br /> And remember, this is just one of your advancement methods. While you're spending experience to pick up Birthrights, or to max out your Skills and Attributes, you're also completing Deeds. And it's that which triggers Legend increasing, and controls Callings and Boons (I.e., where you actually get your big, flashy power).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ok, so there's my problem. I was reading this like an old white wolf book, and instead of reading it as a single cost, I was reading the figure as cost-per-dot. So, raising a skill from 2-3, in the way I was incorrectly reading it, was either 10 or 15 experience points, and raising an attribute from 2-3 was either 20 or 30 experience points. That's why it seemed so high.<br /> <br /> I was simply reading something into the text that wasn't there due to my previous experience with White Wolf games, which this isn't.<br /> <br /> My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8985-gnomeborg","name":"Gnomeborg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-15T10:29:09-07:00","id":1207317,"title":"","content":"Ok, so I'm failing at Paths. Specifically the Contacts section from Origin. Willing to admit that this just might be me not understanding.<br /> <br /> The pertinent paragraph states...<br /> <br /> &quot;A character gains two points per invocation to use to create her Contacts. She can spend these dots on either gaining additional Contacts, or making a single Contact better. Each Contact beings with one dot and one tag (See list of suggested tags below). Each additional point placed in a single Contact adds an additional tag.&quot;<br /> <br /> so, here are my questions<br /> <br /> 1) Do you start with a contact, or do you have to invoke once to get your first contact? I assume the answer is that you start with one.<br /> <br /> 2) Are these bonus dice (points?) permanent? Every session, if a player invokes a contact, that contact gets 2 points better? So, in session 3, each one of my players could have a 5 dot contact with 5 tags? If not, where's the limit? Do the dots go away? If so, when? If the player has 3 paths and a Guide, can they invoke all 4 of their paths 3 times in the same session and end up with 4 7 dot Contacts with 7 tags each?<br /> <br /> 3) How many times can you invoke a contact? The book says both Once Per Session, and then a few pages later it says Twice Per Session or maybe more if you're willing to pay the consequences. Additionally, this sentence appears: &quot;Each connection may only be called upon twice in a single session. If the Path has already been invoked twice this session, you can still invoke it for more dots.&quot; So, the connection can only be called upon twice? But the connections are supposed to be distinct from the contacts. I'd buy that this isn't supposed to be talking about contacts at all, but then it talks about adding dots, which is a specific mechanic of Contacts and not discussed associated as anything else. Also it talks about if the Path has been invoked twice already. Any time you call upon your path whether it is to call upon a contact or connections, or add dice to a relevant roll, or gaining access to anything relevant, that's described as Invoking your path. So the thing you're supposed to always have access to you can only do twice per session? But again, it goes on to talk about adding dots, which is something that's only a mechanic of Contacts.<br /> <br /> 4) Do guides, which can be invoked just like Paths, function under the same rules of creating contacts? I assume yes, because it doesn't say differently. So, a character's Guide can give them more contacts as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8985-gnomeborg","user":"Gnomeborg","date":". 04-15-2018, 01:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8985-gnomeborg","name":"Gnomeborg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8985_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-16T10:54:07-07:00","id":1207705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomeborg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1207317#post1207317\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so I'm failing at Paths. Specifically the Contacts section from Origin. Willing to admit that this just might be me not understanding.<br /> <br /> The pertinent paragraph states...<br /> <br /> &quot;A character gains two points per invocation to use to create her Contacts. She can spend these dots on either gaining additional Contacts, or making a single Contact better. Each Contact beings with one dot and one tag (See list of suggested tags below). Each additional point placed in a single Contact adds an additional tag.&quot;<br /> <br /> so, here are my questions<br /> <br /> 1) Do you start with a contact, or do you have to invoke once to get your first contact? I assume the answer is that you start with one.<br /> <br /> 2) Are these bonus dice (points?) permanent? Every session, if a player invokes a contact, that contact gets 2 points better? So, in session 3, each one of my players could have a 5 dot contact with 5 tags? If not, where's the limit? Do the dots go away? If so, when? If the player has 3 paths and a Guide, can they invoke all 4 of their paths 3 times in the same session and end up with 4 7 dot Contacts with 7 tags each?<br /> <br /> 3) How many times can you invoke a contact? The book says both Once Per Session, and then a few pages later it says Twice Per Session or maybe more if you're willing to pay the consequences. Additionally, this sentence appears: &quot;Each connection may only be called upon twice in a single session. If the Path has already been invoked twice this session, you can still invoke it for more dots.&quot; So, the connection can only be called upon twice? But the connections are supposed to be distinct from the contacts. I'd buy that this isn't supposed to be talking about contacts at all, but then it talks about adding dots, which is a specific mechanic of Contacts and not discussed associated as anything else. Also it talks about if the Path has been invoked twice already. Any time you call upon your path whether it is to call upon a contact or connections, or add dice to a relevant roll, or gaining access to anything relevant, that's described as Invoking your path. So the thing you're supposed to always have access to you can only do twice per session? But again, it goes on to talk about adding dots, which is something that's only a mechanic of Contacts.<br /> <br /> 4) Do guides, which can be invoked just like Paths, function under the same rules of creating contacts? I assume yes, because it doesn't say differently. So, a character's Guide can give them more contacts as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>This actually got answered on the Discord and I think on the Ask Neall thread... I've been collecting an FAQ <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1etYiuHfHR-nTI5obsKhL44stbRmLkuvw2Z6qae_lbWM\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> But to answer your questions to the best of my ability...<br /> <br /> 1) I believe it's assumed you have the contacts in a nebulous sense and you establish them when you Invoke your Path.<br /> <br /> 2) Neall clarified this: The dots gained from Invoking a Contact only last until the end of the session. This prevents the Contact from gaining approximately ALL of the Tags on them.<br /> <br /> 3) I can only assume the first Once Per Session was a mistake, as there are rule establishing when you do it twice or more in a session. Maybe an artifact of an earlier ruleset.<br /> <br /> 4) That makes sense. The Guide goes &quot;Don't worry, I know a guy&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-21T21:25:21-07:00","id":1209891,"title":"","content":"So here is a good question. What are the skills for 2e? Or abilities if you are going by 1e's rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T00:02:58-07:00","id":1209932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1209891#post1209891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So here is a good question. What are the skills for 2e? Or abilities if you are going by 1e's rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming you don't have the Manuscript so the snarky answer of &quot;They start on Origins, Page 60&quot; won't help.<ul><li>Academics - Book Learning, particularly the Humanities like legal, political, and bureaucratic systems. Also contributes to how many languages you can be fluent in.</li> <li>Athletics - Physical training and conditioning. Determines how much you can lift, and also is used for making attacks with bows and javelins.</li> <li>Culture - Represents your understanding of different societies and cultures. Encompasses understanding of art, literature, and religious practices from around the world.</li> <li>Close Combat - Used for hitting people who are in your face. Due to the mutable nature of the skills, can also be used for knowing about fighting styles.</li> <li>Empathy - Social Awareness. Helps you understand other people.</li> <li>Firearms - For all your gun-based needs. Mostly for shooting, but could also be used to represent how well you know your guns.</li> <li>Integrity - Your ability to resist emotional influence. Often used to resist mind control effects.</li> <li>Leadership - Your ability to lead and coordinate groups. If you're taking the position of say, a project director, you'll need this.</li> <li>Medicine - For figuring out how someone's hurting and how to fix it.</li> <li>Occult - Your knowledge of the supernatural, and the spooky scary things. Good for monsters, rituals, and knowing the histories of the various pantheons.</li> <li>Persuasion - How easily you can influence people, one-on-one.</li> <li>Pilot - Your ability to make an object of transportation work, whether it be a car, a motorcycle, a horse, or a jet.</li> <li>Science - Your understanding of the Scientific Method and your ability to parse out evidence from observations. Note that you can use this with Occultic stuff, such as using tissue tests to see what the weakness of this monster may be.</li> <li>Subterfuge - Ability to deceive others, hide, and create disguises. If you're doing stuff the cops wouldn't approve of and it's not murder, you'll be using THIS a lot.</li> <li>Survival - Your knowledge of the general outdoors. Navigation, scavenging, putting together simple tools from resources around, taming local wildlife... D&amp;D Ranger Skills.</li> <li>Technology - Your understanding of modern devices. Equally good for computers and other electronics, or fixing giant machines. Note that this skill may differ in era-specific games.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T03:27:29-07:00","id":1209964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1209932#post1209932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming you don't have the Manuscript so the snarky answer of &quot;They start on Origins, Page 60&quot; won't help.<ul><li>Academics - Book Learning, particularly the Humanities like legal, political, and bureaucratic systems. Also contributes to how many languages you can be fluent in.</li> <li>Athletics - Physical training and conditioning. Determines how much you can lift, and also is used for making attacks with bows and javelins.</li> <li>Culture - Represents your understanding of different societies and cultures. Encompasses understanding of art, literature, and religious practices from around the world.</li> <li>Close Combat - Used for hitting people who are in your face. Due to the mutable nature of the skills, can also be used for knowing about fighting styles.</li> <li>Empathy - Social Awareness. Helps you understand other people.</li> <li>Firearms - For all your gun-based needs. Mostly for shooting, but could also be used to represent how well you know your guns.</li> <li>Integrity - Your ability to resist emotional influence. Often used to resist mind control effects.</li> <li>Leadership - Your ability to lead and coordinate groups. If you're taking the position of say, a project director, you'll need this.</li> <li>Medicine - For figuring out how someone's hurting and how to fix it.</li> <li>Occult - Your knowledge of the supernatural, and the spooky scary things. Good for monsters, rituals, and knowing the histories of the various pantheons.</li> <li>Persuasion - How easily you can influence people, one-on-one.</li> <li>Pilot - Your ability to make an object of transportation work, whether it be a car, a motorcycle, a horse, or a jet.</li> <li>Science - Your understanding of the Scientific Method and your ability to parse out evidence from observations. Note that you can use this with Occultic stuff, such as using tissue tests to see what the weakness of this monster may be.</li> <li>Subterfuge - Ability to deceive others, hide, and create disguises. If you're doing stuff the cops wouldn't approve of and it's not murder, you'll be using THIS a lot.</li> <li>Survival - Your knowledge of the general outdoors. Navigation, scavenging, putting together simple tools from resources around, taming local wildlife... D&amp;D Ranger Skills.</li> <li>Technology - Your understanding of modern devices. Equally good for computers and other electronics, or fixing giant machines. Note that this skill may differ in era-specific games.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Well you would be right. I do not have the origins document. So therefore good sir I shall give you some snark in return for the snark you were not able to give me and we shall all then be in snark heaven for it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Which me knowing the page number would do me about as much good as knowing what is the price of tea in China. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So then it seems like they made some of the skills far more specialized and flat out dropped others. Science is now the old Investigation skill and Bows and Arrows are under...Athletics now? *raises an eyebrow* So where does it cover about throwing weapons?<br /> <br /> Pilot is now the old Control skill? Don't honestly see the point of that change but w/e.<br /> <br /> Anyway thank you for the listing. Do the gods in the new system have the favored skills like in the old system or was that part dropped for the all fancy doodads the new system is toting around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-22T05:42:46-07:00","id":1209987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1209964#post1209964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well you would be right. I do not have the origins document. So therefore good sir I shall give you some snark in return for the snark you were not able to give me and we shall all then be in snark heaven for it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Which me knowing the page number would do me about as much good as knowing what is the price of tea in China. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So then it seems like they made some of the skills far more specialized and flat out dropped others. Science is now the old Investigation skill and Bows and Arrows are under...Athletics now? *raises an eyebrow* So where does it cover about throwing weapons?<br /> <br /> Pilot is now the old Control skill? Don't honestly see the point of that change but w/e.<br /> <br /> Anyway thank you for the listing. Do the gods in the new system have the favored skills like in the old system or was that part dropped for the all fancy doodads the new system is toting around?</div> </div> </div> </div>Investigation can be done through whichever Skill is the most relevant to the crime scene... Checking a dead body can be done through Medicine, figuring out what kind of tires left behind these tracks would require Pilot and deciphering the meaning of the mystic runes drawn in blood at the crime scene would require Occult.<br /> <br /> Athletics covers thrown weapons as well as bows.<br /> <br /> They did indeed decide that the new doodads were incentive enough, and individual Gods no longer have favoured skills. Instead, each Pantheon has a pair of Skills that it favours, and Scions of that Pantheon automatically start with a minimum of one dot in those two Skills. So children of the Aesir have a minimum knowledge of punching things and reading the strands of Fate, in the form of Close Combat and Occult, children of the Shen gain a minimum competency in pushing papers and ordering people around, in the form of Academics and Leadership, children of the Deva learn how to rough it and shoot people full of arrows with Survival and Athletics, and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 04-22-2018, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T04:50:43-07:00","id":1210367,"title":"","content":"Also how did they change the Epic Attributes in this system? Is that still like it was in the old system where your parent deity gave you certain affinities but you were free to pick and choose which ones you wanted to do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T05:05:34-07:00","id":1210370,"title":"","content":"The physical epic attribute are now purviews. Think on how hercules is literally considered a god of strength so in his purviews et get epic strength. The rest are kind of gone, as in you dont get them named anywhere. But now all knacks are in the Callings so you'll find the epic attributes knack there. For example the Sage calling is a good place to find the equivalent of the intelligence knacks, etc, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T05:26:14-07:00","id":1210373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1210367#post1210367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also how did they change the Epic Attributes in this system? Is that still like it was in the old system where your parent deity gave you certain affinities but you were free to pick and choose which ones you wanted to do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Epic Attributes don't really exist, at least not in the way they used to... The three Epic Physicals are Purviews now, Epic Appearance is now the Beauty Purview, and most of the powers that would have been in the other Attributes are spread across the eleven Callings, which describe essentially the <i>kind</i> of God or mythic archetype of a Hero you're aiming to be... These are Creator, Guardian, Healer, Hunter, Judge, Leader, Liminal, Lover, Sage, Trickster and Warrior.<br /> <br /> Each God has a list of three Callings. Each Scion must share at least one Calling with their parent starting out. You also get any single one of your parent's Purviews to channel innately (along with the signature pantheon Purview of course) that you don't need birthrights to channel. That's it. You no longer get any XP discounts, so you're completely free to follow any Purview you choose without penalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 04-23-2018, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-23T20:19:05-07:00","id":1210778,"title":"","content":"So how did the change the Pantheon Specific Purviews for the new system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T01:39:22-07:00","id":1210864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1210778#post1210778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So how did the change the Pantheon Specific Purviews for the new system?</div> </div> </div> </div>They function just like normal Purviews... They each have a passive power that you get just for having access to them (and you always have access to your PSP) and beyond that you have Boons in them that you can use as normal. They can also be used to work Marvels (free form Purview magic) just like all Purviews can. <br /> <br /> Some of the PSPs have changed themes since 1e though... The Aesir now have Wyrd, their own brand of Fate magic instead of Jotunblut; the Theoi have a penchant for shape shifting through their Purview of Metamorphosis; the Teotl PSP has evolved into being about both accepting AND repaying sacrifice, and is called Nextlahualli, Repayment of Debt; the Deva focus on the pathways of union with the divine that is Yoga; the Shen now focus on the Bureaucracy of Heaven through their Purview of Tianming; and the Manitou, being new this edition, are rocking the dream quests and spirits of Dodaem.<br /> <br /> The Orisha still have Possession as a PSP; the Kami still have Eight Million Kami, which has had its name changed but is doing the same thing as the 1e Purview; the Netjer are still working with the soul and name magic of Heku; the Tuatha, finally, are channeling Geasa and Bardic Knowledge through their PSP of Geasa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-24T04:23:40-07:00","id":1210894,"title":"","content":"Ah good I was wondering how they were going to do the Aesir. Their pantheon specific purview in 1e pretty much sucked balls as far as I was concerned. It was honestly the most useless of PSPs. The Japanese and the Greeks and the Loa were some of the more useful ones. The Egyptian and Aztecs fell somewhere in the middle. I'm not as familiar with the other pantheons to say one way or the other who might be better but meh like I said the Norse pantheon was pretty useless in my opinion. The whole &quot;I give you my blood and make mortal stronger but now as strong as me.&quot; was kind of a bit of a let down.<br /> <br /> Though the Greeks having shape shifting is...not exactly as useful as the old Arte purview could be, but meh at least the way they did it this time around I can safely say this is a change I am actually pretty okay with. This was a good change for the system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:45:41-07:00","id":1211824,"title":"","content":"This has probably already been answered in some other thread, but I don't have the will to go through 3000 posts of Ask Neall so I'll risk being redundant and ask here: Purviews like Artistry and Beasts have both general and specific iterations, with a nice bonus for choosing to be specific. When your divine patron has a specific purview--say, &quot;Beasts (Horses)&quot;-- and you want to take it as your inherent purview...<br /> <br /> a) you must take the specific purview associated with your parent<br /> b) you may take either the general purview or the specific purview associated with your parent<br /> c) you may take the general purview or any specific purview you like<br /> d) none of the above?<br /> <br /> I have a hunch it's (a), but I haven't found anywhere that it says for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:56:07-07:00","id":1211830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1211824#post1211824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably already been answered in some other thread, but I don't have the will to go through 3000 posts of Ask Neall so I'll risk being redundant and ask here: Purviews like Artistry and Beasts have both general and specific iterations, with a nice bonus for choosing to be specific. When your divine patron has a specific purview--say, &quot;Beasts (Horses)&quot;-- and you want to take it as your inherent purview...<br /> <br /> a) you must take the specific purview associated with your parent<br /> b) you may take either the general purview or the specific purview associated with your parent<br /> c) you may take the general purview or any specific purview you like<br /> d) none of the above?<br /> <br /> I have a hunch it's (a), but I haven't found anywhere that it says for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't remember where Neall answered this, but it's c).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24028-mike-mccall","name":"Mike McCall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:56:57-07:00","id":1211833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1211824#post1211824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably already been answered in some other thread, but I don't have the will to go through 3000 posts of Ask Neall so I'll risk being redundant and ask here: Purviews like Artistry and Beasts have both general and specific iterations, with a nice bonus for choosing to be specific. When your divine patron has a specific purview--say, &quot;Beasts (Horses)&quot;-- and you want to take it as your inherent purview...<br /> <br /> a) you must take the specific purview associated with your parent<br /> b) you may take either the general purview or the specific purview associated with your parent<br /> c) you may take the general purview or any specific purview you like<br /> d) none of the above?<br /> <br /> I have a hunch it's (a), but I haven't found anywhere that it says for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>C... you are not in any way bound by your Parent's specialization, so you can have general Beasts or Beasts (Possums) even if your parent has Beasts (Horses).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T08:58:04-07:00","id":1211834,"title":"","content":"Nice! Thanks for the clarification.<br /> <br /> Edit: So why list the parent's specialization at all? Just for flavor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T09:18:53-07:00","id":1211841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1211834#post1211834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice! Thanks for the clarification.<br /> <br /> Edit: So why list the parent's specialization at all? Just for flavor?</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people might want to know what sort of animals a specific deity is related to, both for use as a Storyteller, but also for a Player. Stuff like thinking what Creatures they could grant thematically, or clothing with decals related to that animal, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T10:42:24-07:00","id":1211885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1211824#post1211824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably already been answered in some other thread, but I don't have the will to go through 3000 posts of Ask Neall so I'll risk being redundant and ask here: Purviews like Artistry and Beasts have both general and specific iterations, with a nice bonus for choosing to be specific. When your divine patron has a specific purview--say, &quot;Beasts (Horses)&quot;-- and you want to take it as your inherent purview...<br /> <br /> a) you must take the specific purview associated with your parent<br /> b) you may take either the general purview or the specific purview associated with your parent<br /> c) you may take the general purview or any specific purview you like<br /> d) none of the above?<br /> <br /> I have a hunch it's (a), but I haven't found anywhere that it says for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it's C. Page 284 in the Hero preview says when you pick the Purview, you can choose to narrow the focus to one type of animal. There is a similar note for Artistry and Passion, in their sections.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23791-ashnak","name":"Ashnak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-26T13:46:46-07:00","id":1211960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1211824#post1211824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has probably already been answered in some other thread, but I don't have the will to go through 3000 posts of Ask Neall so I'll risk being redundant and ask here: Purviews like Artistry and Beasts have both general and specific iterations, with a nice bonus for choosing to be specific. When your divine patron has a specific purview--say, &quot;Beasts (Horses)&quot;-- and you want to take it as your inherent purview...<br /> <br /> a) you must take the specific purview associated with your parent<br /> b) you may take either the general purview or the specific purview associated with your parent<br /> c) you may take the general purview or any specific purview you like<br /> d) none of the above?<br /> <br /> I have a hunch it's (a), but I haven't found anywhere that it says for sure.</div> </div> </div> </div>C, actually. A Scion of Inari can take Beast (Jaguar) or a Scion of Ama-no-Uzume can take Artistry General rather than (Dancing), AFAIK<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh hey a &quot;Next Page&quot; button","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":".  Hella Ninja'd 04-26-2018, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T01:52:35-07:00","id":1212181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1211834#post1211834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: So why list the parent's specialization at all? Just for flavor?</div> </div> </div> </div> You aren't the only one who is asking that question. Why even bother listing it if it doesn't do anything or impact the scion in any meaningful and mechanical way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T06:08:07-07:00","id":1212245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1212181#post1212181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You aren't the only one who is asking that question. Why even bother listing it if it doesn't do anything or impact the scion in any meaningful and mechanical way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may not be mechanical, but that doesn't make it any less meaningful. Knowing that Poseidon is a God of Horses is just as important as knowing that he's a God of the Seas. Knowing that Shiva only has Artistry (Dance) and his sister Sarasvati has Artistry (All) is an important distinction to make to understand what kind of things those Gods do. They can provide fodder for Birthright ideas, as a Creature or Followers, and even more importantly, they can inform interactions with your God... how does Bast feel that her child went and picked up Beasts (Dog)? What does Parvati think of the daughter who spreads Passion (Hate)? Does staid old Confucius even consider his son's Artistry (Tap Dancing) a worthy calling to pursue? The Specializations help to give them a bit more flavour, which is never a bad thing in a role-playing game, especially in a game about Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T07:54:34-07:00","id":1212276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samudra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1212245#post1212245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may not be mechanical, but that doesn't make it any less meaningful. Knowing that Poseidon is a God of Horses is just as important as knowing that he's a God of the Seas. Knowing that Shiva only has Artistry (Dance) and his sister Sarasvati has Artistry (All) is an important distinction to make to understand what kind of things those Gods do. They can provide fodder for Birthright ideas, as a Creature or Followers, and even more importantly, they can inform interactions with your God... how does Bast feel that her child went and picked up Beasts (Dog)? What does Parvati think of the daughter who spreads Passion (Hate)? Does staid old Confucius even consider his son's Artistry (Tap Dancing) a worthy calling to pursue? The Specializations help to give them a bit more flavour, which is never a bad thing in a role-playing game, especially in a game about Gods.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true that there is value in knowing the symbolism associated with a god, but there is space provided for it (and I realize this is an odd place to be picking nits, but since the discussion is ongoing...). There is plenty of room in the descriptions of the gods to explain the traditional associations and symbolism of their purviews. Poseidon is clearly described as a god of seas, earthquakes and horses, so players and STs who want to build symbolic systems around him have access to that information. <br /> <br /> The list of purviews (at least in Hero) is a piece of mechanical, chargen-focused information. We don't expect every facet of the god to be fully and exclusively represented by their list of purviews, so having that piece of extraneous information in that part of the god's write-up adds confusion more than resolving it. I mean, that confusion is resolved easily enough by having the rule clarified, so it's not a huge deal, but as a matter of style it's a bit of an irritant.<br /> <br /> Of course, in Demigod and God, when the gods are more near and active entities that PCs can interact with, the gods' purview specifiers may become relevant information, but they aren't yet.<br /> <br /> On a different subject, I also have a question about relic design: Where is the line between situation and general when it comes to enhancement bonuses. The specific example I have is a relic car with amazing handling such that it gives an enhancement bonus to Pilot rolls when you're driving it. To me, this feels pretty general, but it's significantly less general than, say, a pair of relic driving gloves that give you an enhancement bonus to all Pilot rolls you make no matter what you're driving (or flying). And if we say that driving the relic car is situational, does that mean that a relic sword that gives you a bonus to Close Combat rolls when you fight with it is also situational? Because that seems potentially even more abuseable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T08:16:28-07:00","id":1212288,"title":"","content":"I believe the answer is actually C.<br /> <br /> e: oh hey new page, didn't see you there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1778-morsrattus","name":"MorsRattus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1778_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"189"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-27T22:41:56-07:00","id":1212541,"title":"","content":"I still find it hard to believe Japan as a nation developed a culture and mythology that was totally devoid of fire in any form.<br /> <br /> Now then on a different subject. You mentioned how the Norse now have some fate magic type stuff going on. How exactly does that part work? I am kind of curious as it's a change I think they needed to make them better able to compete with the other pantheons.<br /> <br /> Which also brings me to the question of how does the Shen work as well? I know the one in 1e was based on the concept of Ying/Yang. But this one focuses on Bureaucracy? Which if that's the case then oh boy it looks like Harry Dresden's comment about Bureaumancers is true. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which kuddos to anyone who got the reference if not well...go read the Dresden Files. Best book series evvva! Oh yeah. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T00:52:43-07:00","id":1212557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1212541#post1212541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still find it hard to believe Japan as a nation developed a culture and mythology that was totally devoid of fire in any form.</div> </div> </div> </div>Erm... it wasn't? They have Kagutsuchi and Kojin, whom you've mentioned yourself on these forums... why do you suddenly think their culture was devoid of fire?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1212541#post1212541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now then on a different subject. You mentioned how the Norse now have some fate magic type stuff going on. How exactly does that part work? I am kind of curious as it's a change I think they needed to make them better able to compete with the other pantheons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd lets the Norse Gods Read the Runes and spin out Blessings and Curses to through the art of Seidr. The Innate gives you your own Fated Destiny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1212541#post1212541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which also brings me to the question of how does the Shen work as well? I know the one in 1e was based on the concept of Ying/Yang. But this one focuses on Bureaucracy? Which if that's the case then oh boy it looks like Harry Dresden's comment about Bureaumancers is true. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Tianming lets the Chinese Gods give people Titles and functions within the vast Bureaucracy of Heaven and put curses on bureaucracies and organizations to clog them up. The Innate lets you ignore bureaucratic complications and delays for yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T04:29:38-07:00","id":1212596,"title":"","content":"The comment I made about the Japanese was meant to be a bit derisive about the fact that the creators seemed to ignore this fact just out of hand for it. When it's been proven in many parts of the mythology they did in fact have gods dedicated to fire. Both in Kojin and Kagustuchi. Fire has also been attributed to Inari as well. So continuing to deny them the Fire purview seems to just be kind of lame and stupid me.<br /> <br /> Now then other parts hehe... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Okay....then. I was right. So it is official the Shen are now effectively Bureaumancers. That's...I'm not sure how to answer how to feel about that change. Not in a bad way. Just as an idea and concept. I was laughing my ass off about the whole thing.(Again in the good kind of way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> As for the Norse...yeah okay that is actually kind of cool to be honest with you. Again this is something they really needed and seems to fit them a bit more than the old one. (I'm also kind of a bit of a lover of rune magic. So...yeah... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T04:44:27-07:00","id":1212599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1212596#post1212596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The comment I made about the Japanese was meant to be a bit derisive about the fact that the creators seemed to ignore this fact just out of hand for it. When it's been proven in many parts of the mythology they did in fact have gods dedicated to fire. Both in Kojin and Kagustuchi. Fire has also been attributed to Inari as well. So continuing to deny them the Fire purview seems to just be kind of lame and stupid me.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have limited page space and the Kami have Eight Million members (and yes I'm aware that is not a literal number). It's kind of silly to expect them to include every single God, and even sillier to expect them to write up the Pantheons with regards to some kind of 'we have to include all the Purviews' mindset, which is doomed to failure anyway since not every Purview exists as an important enough concept in every mythology... The Deva write-up has no God with Forge and their Moon God is also not statted... that doesn't mean Vishwakarma or Chandra don't exist or that the authors don't know that they exist, just that they had limited space and decided they weren't important enough to include. Additional Gods for each Pantheon will be included in the Companion, so if the developers feel that either Kagutsuchi or Kojin need to be in, they might find a place there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1344,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","user":"Samudra","date":". 04-28-2018, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T05:41:32-07:00","id":1212609,"title":"","content":"Which I get that they didn't have a lot of space to work with and they were crunch for time and other such technical jargon that goes waaaaayyyyy above both our pay grades(Don't know how much you get paid. If it's more than me well um..yeah kudos for having a better job <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> My biggest beef was leaving out the purview as a whole. That seems to me to be a huge disservice to them. While yes them leaving out the deities is a bit annoying I would have been fine if they stuck the purview in somewhere with someone. As I mentioned before someone like Inari or even maybe Amaterasu since well on a few occasions sun gods you get fire in the same boat. Which you know kudos they elevated Inari in 2e.<br /> <br /> She was like the equivalent of a minor noble we'll say in 1e. Which if they put the word fire in there I'm pretty sure they could have found a way to reduce the number of letter &quot;a&quot;s or even letter &quot;I&quot;s through through the book. Or even even use one or two smaller words that would fit. Which is the way they use to make new &quot;editions&quot; for college text books. Yeah they go in and make six changes in the overall like 300+ page book and call it a new edition. Which said changes can include changing a word or two here and there. Again it's the total lack of the purview that's been more my beef than anything else. Which this even extends as far back as 1e when I noticed it.<br /> <br /> So it's not just with 2e that I have the issue. No it's a problem in 1e as well. That's always been my problem. It just kind of irks me that they don't bother with it even in the first printing. First off the new edition should say everything you mean to say and then you release supplementary material after that. Giving them the fire purview in the first book and the later adding the fire deities would pretty much solve my issue on that problem.<br /> <br /> A case in point of a pantheon that doesn't have a purview that bothered me a bit less was the Aztecs missing the Chaos purview in 1e. I was a bit less bothered that as 1) I have much less of an interest in Aztec mythology and 2) In a sense them not having such a purview just seemed right from the way they did things. The Aztecs were all about cosmic order and such stuff. So someone having the Chaos thing...was kind of the antithesis of what the pantheon stood for. Their big thing to put it in a nut shell was making sure the trains ran on time as the saying goes. Just on a cosmic scale.<br /> <br /> Anyway sorry for the off-tangent rant there about the Aztecs. Again love the new Aesir PSP and to a slightly lesser extent the Shen's PSP. They're Bureaumancers, ahh god that still cracks me up. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Which is only slightly less insidious to the old Tai-yi or whatever it was called PSP the Shen had in 1e. That one could get broken pretty damn fast from what I read of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","user":"Sessha","date":". 04-28-2018, 08:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T06:48:28-07:00","id":1212638,"title":"","content":"Sessha, I'll let you in on a secret.<br /> <br /> Gods are stupidly easy to stat up yourself. Pick three appropriate feeling Callings, maybe by reading their Wikipedia page, and pick a handful of Purviews. You want your Fire-Innate Kami Scion, you can make Kojin yourself.<br /> <br /> Also, literally nothing stops you from getting Fire through a Relic or a Guide. This isn't like 1e, where going outside the specialties of your parents hits you with a major XP tax. You want a burning sword for your divine Samurai? Go nuts. You want Kojin as a Guide to teach your Scion the mysteries of the sacred flame? Aces.<br /> <br /> But majorly... The Patrons list in the writeups is in no way, shape, or form meant to be comprehensive. In an earlier draft of the Deva Pantheon, Kali didn't have an entry, with intentions to add her later.<br /> <br /> Then our own Samudra wrote a great bio for her on this forum and it was used as a base for her entry in the Hero book, IIRC","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 04-28-2018, 09:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T07:12:43-07:00","id":1212646,"title":"","content":"I do thank you for the advice. I do really thank you. As much as I have said before most of 2e has left a bitter taste in mouth. The only two things so far that have REALLY REALLY REALLY impressed with was the retooling of the Aesir and lesser extent the Shen PSPs. Again I can't express how badly they needed a retooling of their PSP. It was just so...useless in 1e. Did I mention how much love the new Aesir PSP? It makes me want to play a scion of the Aesir if just for that particular purview alone. And the Shen..bureaumancers! All I'm going to say on that one. Bureaumancers. Yes I'm still laughing about the concept(in a gleeful happy sort of way.) Mostly because well it's just so out there a concept that it's honestly kind of funny. Again in a good way.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-08T11:30:28-07:00","id":1216749,"title":"","content":"So this is a small one, hell I dunno if it should be posted here...<br /> <br /> Page 102 of the Hero Manuscript, where it's talking about the cosmology of the Manitou, it has a typo in the second paragraph under &quot;Underworld&quot;. &quot;Terra Incognitia&quot; instead of &quot;Terra Incognita&quot;. Might want to edit that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T15:05:03-07:00","id":1236916,"title":"","content":"So a mechanics question. You all mentioned to me about the Aesir's new PSP being something about runic based. How exactly is that suppose to work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23711-sessha","name":"Sessha","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T15:30:34-07:00","id":1236923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sessha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1195852-the-scion-hero-error-question-thread?p=1236916#post1236916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a mechanics question. You all mentioned to me about the Aesir's new PSP being something about runic based. How exactly is that suppose to work?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not their PSP, that's their Pantheon Motif. Slight difference.<br /> <br /> You know how in 1e if you didn't have the right Boon to do something with your Purview you were SOL? There's a sidestep to that with what are called Marvels. Freeform but more expensive divine workings.<br /> <br /> Each Pantheon has a Motif with which to work these Marvels, each one drawing in what each base culture considers to be their magical tradition.<br /> <br /> For example, a Scion of the Aesir can work Marvels through their Motif of weaving magic or use of runes. So if your Scion of Skadi wants to use the Frost Purview to cause a snowstorm to block out traffic or something. They could whip out a loom or another weaving tool like a distaff to weave Fate to influence the weather, or carve tunes into a nearby hill to bring in a mysterious cold front, without a Boon.<br /> <br /> The Tuatha Motif is &quot;Magic flows from Verse and Satire&quot;, so a Tuatha Scion with Epic Dex could chant a poem about how they're so light on their feet that they can run on the wind to imitate the effects of the flight Boon despite not having it. Though at a higher cost.<br /> <br /> Edit: As for the Aesir's PSP... Wyrd is about how the Aesir have a VERY heavy tie to Fates, personal and grand. I mean, a big part of their drama is that they know how the world ends and how they die, and the harder they struggle the tighter this fate pulls.<br /> <br /> Wyrd's innate power is &quot;Something terrible is going to happen to you. Gain momentum when trying to avoid this gets you in trouble, or if you come across circumstances that echo it&quot;. It has Boons that let you basically cast runes or weave or do something to predict the future and gain bonuses to help bring it about, and one that can be used to spell out doom for those you curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 07-19-2018, 09:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}